    "The model systematically overshoots peak levels by 5-8% in the first 7 days after a recent price spike, ignoring volatility expansion signals.",
    "True outcomes often reverse within 3-5 days of the forecast start date, whereas the model assumes stability or continuation for the full 30-day horizon.",
    "In high-volatility regimes (price swings >10% in 18 days), the model's linear extrapolation ignores the 'mean-reverting' behavior typical of EU ETS carbon prices."
